{"stats":{"took":169,"total":1,"estimate":false,"maxScore":153.12604},"results":[{"_meta":{"score":153.12604},"copyright":{"thirdPartyPermissionsProduced":false,"disclosedToPublic":false,"containsIndication":false,"publisherPermissionOrRightsToDistribute":false,"belongsToUsGov":false,"determinationType":"PUBLIC_USE_PERMITTED","thirdPartyContentCondition":"NOT_SET","belongsToContractor":false,"disclosedInvention":false,"submissionId":20240008508,"containsThirdPartyMaterial":false,"belongsToPublisher":false,"id":"c87b6c56d4c74b15b1da92053d8e28f7","belongsToAuthors":false},"subjectCategories":["Aerospace Medicine"],"exportControl":{"isExportControl":"NO","submissionId":20240008508,"ear":"NO","id":"142e84c1ccc2448c878ae454afeeff10","itar":"NO"},"distributionDate":"2024-07-17T05:00:00.0000000+00:00","fundingNumbers":[{"number":"251546.06","submissionId":20240008508,"id":"defbff4c427a42e1826ad46397b56573","type":"WBS"}],"title":"Crew Health and Performance Integrated Data Architecture (CHP-IDA) TechPort May 2024","stiType":"OTHER","distribution":"PUBLIC","submittedDate":"2024-07-03T18:10:13.4202830+00:00","authorAffiliations":[{"organizationId":"fdea3daf3b5156699f511edf3e9b9ec4","sequence":0,"submissionId":20240008508,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Courtney M Schkurko"},"organization":{"name":"Glenn Research Center","location":"Cleveland, United States"}},"id":"c53f2077ac9a498a928232fe48fefacd","userType":"CIVIL","userId":"fac9a169645e4fb7a7c8d8a7481dcef8"},{"organizationId":"30956d12b05c56f99ba04cefabd82400","sequence":1,"submissionId":20240008508,"meta":{"author":{"orcidId":"","name":"Justin D Yang"},"organization":{"name":"KBR (United States)","location":"Houston, Texas, United States"}},"id":"7aeec25146d849499e83154cdabde5ff","userType":"CONTRACTOR_GRANTEE","userId":"5a34d6ded4fa4e7eadcf0ccd107eab7e"},{"organizationId":"4c6a2b878d76521da887cdcb2564bf90","sequence":2,"submissionId":20240008508,"meta":{"author":{"orcidId":"","name":"Moriah Shay Thompson"},"organization":{"name":"Johnson Space Center","location":"Houston, United States"}},"id":"15b19a502ed745d0bbce08defd6686d6","userType":"CIVIL","userId":"24c6035bc2e44aaa8ea0b792a95decdc"},{"organizationId":"4c6a2b878d76521da887cdcb2564bf90","sequence":3,"submissionId":20240008508,"meta":{"author":{"orcidId":"","name":"Rahul Suresh"},"organization":{"name":"Johnson Space Center","location":"Houston, United States"}},"id":"ac24e8db299b487696ebb44c7b71d737","userType":"CIVIL","userId":"ed0947a3b1674e0eaef5d58fff6e8430"}],"stiTypeDetails":"Other - Techport Entry","technicalReviewType":"NASA_TECHNICAL_MANAGEMENT","modified":"2025-08-31T18:39:21.7150190+00:00","id":20240008508,"created":"2024-07-03T18:04:26.5020770+00:00","center":{"code":"JSC","name":"Johnson Space Center","id":"dd46994b91a94cb2a2722617cbbadc55"},"onlyAbstract":false,"sensitiveInformation":2,"abstract":"Future exploration missions to Mars will have increased need for crew autonomy. Crew Health & Performance (CHP) related data on the ISS is currently, manually downlinked and in disparate locations, which limits crew autonomy for future missions. The CHP-IDA project is developing a backend data system platform that grants the ability to seamlessly collect, store, process, and display CHP-related data for exploration missions. This platform allows for integration of data and advanced analytics that offer crew and ground teams better insight into the crew’s health and performance. It also enables applications that can improve the crew’s ability to provide more autonomous medical care during exploration missions. Data will be collected automatically to reduce crew and ground team time and effort and will synchronize across all in-mission vehicles, habitats, and ground as communication delay permits.\n\nThe Human Research Program’s (HRP) Medical Data Architecture (MDA) project focused on this backend data architecture but for medical data only. The CHP-IDA project, a joint effort between HRP’s Exploration Medical Capability (ExMC) element and the Exploration Medical Integrated Product Team (XMIPT), expands this capability to all relevant CHP-related data. The additional inputs from nutrition, environment, exercise, radiation, and any other relevant sources will give more insight into crew’s health and performance. Currently, the Human Systems Engineering and Integration Division at Johnson Space Center (JSC) is designing the system. The team completed a system requirements review (SRR) in FY22 and now the focus is on core software development, testbed buildup, and use case scenario demonstration. An end-to-end demonstration with multiple data sources across CHP domains is schedule for the end of FY24 where all three focus areas will be displayed. Following this ground demo, the software will be completed, tested, and validated for flight.","isLessonsLearned":false,"disseminated":"DOCUMENT_AND_METADATA","cui":{"isCui":false,"submissionId":20240008508,"id":"5f68a657f48340d494fc69ba3e9d78a4"},"publications":[{"submissionId":20240008508,"id":"d6017a3430b14d92a85daf4eed5e1722","publicationDate":"2024-07-15T05:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"status":"CURATED","related":[],"downloads":[{"draft":false,"mimetype":"application/pdf","name":"CHP-IDA Techport May 2024.pdf","type":"STI","links":{"original":"/api/citations/20240008508/downloads/CHP-IDA%20Techport%20May%202024.pdf","pdf":"/api/citations/20240008508/downloads/CHP-IDA%20Techport%20May%202024.pdf","fulltext":"/api/citations/20240008508/downloads/CHP-IDA%20Techport%20May%202024.pdf.txt"}}],"downloadsAvailable":true,"index":"submissions-2026-11-12-06-24"}],"aggregations":{"created":{"buckets":[{"key_as_string":"2024","key":1704067200000,"doc_count":1}]},"author":{"doc_count_error_upper_bound":0,"sum_other_doc_count":0,"buckets":[{"key":"Courtney M Schkurko","doc_count":1},{"key":"Justin D Yang","doc_count":1},{"key":"Moriah Shay Thompson","doc_count":1},{"key":"Rahul Suresh","doc_count":1}]},"reportNumber":{"doc_count_error_upper_bound":0,"sum_other_d